      "worked": "The inner function requires $x\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x+1}-1}\\\\f(g(x))&=-\\frac{x+1}{x}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe simplified rule also requires $x\\ne0$. Both restrictions must hold, so $x\\ne-1,0$.\n\nTherefore, the domain is $(-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,0)\\cup(0,\\infty)$.",
